requirements:
Standard sand core specimens (typically 50 mm x 50 mm) prepared with the binder must satisfy minimum physical strength parameters:
a) Early green compression strength (e.g. 0.010 MPa within 15 minutes to prevent core collapse during handling);
b) In-process scratch hardness or mould strength (measured on side walls immediately after stripping);
c) Sustained final compression strength after complete room-temperature curing (attaining a minimum of 1.72 MPa or 17.5 kg/cm² after 240 minutes).
